{"text": "Koutlul\n\n= CONFIDENTIAL -\nRe sum\n\nrnenause ne em\n\nJuly 16, 1979\n\nMr. G. M. Hoefer\nMCA-Graham Advertising\n405 Lexington Avenue\nNew York, New York 10017\n\nDear George:\n\nAs you know, cigarette products can be broadly categorized\nee Several taste profile or \"signature\" groupings. (These\ngroupings are typically found across a company's product\nFoch ings, we have termed the key groupings RJR and PK taste\nsignatures.) We are continuing to investigate and analyse\nthee product situation with the goal of gaining actionable\ninsights.\n\nWe believe there may be similar groupings based on a ci\nWe pet ewnd's image; coming fron its positioning, advertising,\npackaging and name.\u201d Better understanding of these, image\nProupings may lead to effective action; particularly when\nGoupled with product categorizations.\n\nBased on what you know now and MCA-Graham's judgement, would\nyou please analyse cigarette brand imagery to see if useful\ngroupings can be hypothesized. I'd like to get your conclu-\ngroupings fe next four or five weeks. since we hope to address\nthis subject in the next Five Year Plan.\n\nThis request is not meant to make a lot of Agency work.\nRather, our desire is to get some very focused thinking by a\nfou key people that can be boiled down to several pages of\nanalysis.\n\nI'd be pleased to discuss this further.\nBest regards,\nNES.\nRES/j\u00a3 Richard E. Smith\nec: Messrs. J. G. Flinn\n\nT. H. Naw\nF, J, Schultz\n\n2\na\nR\nPy\n3\nir\nx\no\n\n[ADIVISION OF LOEW'S THEATRES. INC\n{656 Fin Avenue, How Yor, New Yor 10019\n\nay",
